"The standard automated Out-of-Context (OOC) flow fails to converge due to a high density of routing 'antennas' and interconnect conflicts at the module boundary. As shown in the table, the automated tool attempts to over-subscribe the physical switchboxes (INT_R tiles), leading to 54 unroutable segments. Furthermore, the tool lacks awareness of the underlying silicon geometry, attempting to place partition pins in non-logic columns (e.g., X26 gaps). Our proposed methodology resolves these bottlenecks by enforcing a One-to-One Interconnect Mapping and aligning the 32-bit data bus to a verified logic column. This results in a 100% routable design, ensuring that the safety-critical navigation kernel can be integrated into the larger SoC without physical design failures."
